    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25qKAJRXdPk6tMQusxFjbvu)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent; safe to merge anytime. Based on `main` (which has #437, the crossref resolver `sp-devonthink-record`; this PR uses it).\n- Stack #415, #418, #419, #420, #421 (still open, so none of their code is on `main`): checked, no overlap in behaviour.\n  - #415 (tags) writes only DEVONthink tags; this PR never touches tags and never merges chapter keywords into them.\n  - #421 (sync) uses the custom metadata field `litnote`; this PR uses the record's `comment`, so they cannot clash.\n  - Conflicts expected only in text: the `sp-devonthink.org` / `.el` key map (`C-c k d`) and the \"Keys\" table, since #415, #418, #420 and #421 also add keys (`t`, `b`, `f`, `a`, `h`, `y`). This PR takes `c` and `C`, which none of them use. Keep both sets of lines.\n- #438 (page labels): not touched; it rewrites the page logic, this PR adds a separate section.\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Problem:** a chapter or section (`incollection`/`inbook` with `crossref`) has no DEVONthink record, so its keywords (what it is about) had no place in DEVONthink.\n- **My reading of the request** (say if wrong):\n  - The chapter's keywords are **not inherited from the parent and not merged into the parent's tags**.\n  - They are stored **on the parent's record, scoped to the chapter**, in a block of the record's `comment`:\n    ```\n    -- sp-chapter: child-2001-x --\n    keywords: value form, Money\n    -- end sp-chapter --\n    ```\n  - Text outside the block is left as it was; writing again replaces only that chapter's block; an empty list removes it.\n  - The chapter's litnote shows them **at the bottom**, under `* Keywords in the book \"Title\" (parent-key)` (`collection` for a collection or proceedings, `book` for a book, `work` otherwise), with `:SP_CHAPTER_OF:` on the heading so re-running rewrites only its body.\n- **Scoping is by text convention only:** only the Emacs code knows a block belongs to one chapter; DEVONthink does not. They do not appear in the tag browser or `tags:` searches (intended).\n- **Open question (decided with Sia: comment only for now):** is a comment enough to find chapter keywords in DEVONthink? The \"Discoverability\" checklist below is there to answer that. Fallback if not: prefixed tags such as `ch:KEY/keyword` (noisier, and the book then carries every chapter's tags).\n- **Source of the keywords:** the `keywords` field of the chapter's BibTeX entry (comma or semicolon separated, duplicates dropped). `C-u` lets you edit them first.\n- **Commands** (`C-c k d`):\n  - `C` `sp-devonthink-chapter-keywords-store`: writes the block to the parent's record. **Asks first**, naming the parent and saying its tags stay as they are.\n  - `c` `sp-devonthink-chapter-keywords-show`: reads the block and puts the section at the bottom of the note. Never writes to DEVONthink; leaves the buffer unsaved.\n  - An entry with a record of its own is refused (its keywords belong on that record).\n- Why `comment`: it is a free text field that exists on every record, is visible in the inspector, and is not used by tags, the `litnote` field or the `#+devonthink:` keyword. A custom metadata field holds one value, so it could not be scoped per chapter without inventing a format inside it anyway.\n- Docs: new \"Chapter keywords\" section in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-devonthink.org` (bullet lists), keys table, testing notes and the open question; `.el` re-tangled. Page-label logic and the offset code untouched.\n- Tests: 40 ERT tests pass on Emacs 29.3 (10 new: block round trip keeping other text, key-prefix safety, asking first, refusing an entry with its own record, show is idempotent and writes nothing). Tangle check passes. `when-let*` style only. No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not tested against DEVONthink.** The AppleScript (`comment of (get record with uuid …)` read and set) was not run; the Org/Emacs logic was tested with the record comment faked.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, fish, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, DEVONthink open on `literature`. Use a throw-away chapter and a parent with a PDF record.\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 441-devonthink-chapter-keywords; git checkout 441-devonthink-chapter-keywords`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -l ert -l tests/sp-devonthink-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 40 pass\n- [ ] In the litnote of a chapter whose BibTeX entry has `keywords` and a `crossref`: `C-c k d C` → prompt names the parent record and says tags stay as they are; answer `n` → \"Cancelled\", the record's comment is unchanged (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Again, answer `y` → \"stored N keyword(s)\"; in DEVONthink's inspector the parent's Comment ends with the `-- sp-chapter: KEY --` block; the parent's tags are unchanged (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Put a line of your own text at the top of the comment, run `C-c k d C` again → your text is untouched, still one block\n- [ ] `C-u C-c k d C`, change the keywords → the block shows the new ones\n- [ ] `C-c k d c` in the note → a `* Keywords in the book \"Title\" (parent-key)` section at the bottom with the keywords; buffer is modified, not saved; run it again → still one section\n- [ ] Do the same for a second chapter of the same parent: two blocks in the comment, each note shows only its own keywords\n- [ ] Edge: a chapter with no `keywords` field: `C-c k d C` says to use `C-u`; a note whose entry has its own record: both commands refuse\n- [ ] Regression: `C-c k d o` on a chapter note still opens the parent record; the parent's tags and the parent's own litnote are unchanged\n\n### Discoverability in DEVONthink (comment only)\n\nUse two chapters of one parent with different keywords, e.g. chapter A `value form`, chapter B `money`, both stored with `C-c k d C`. Pick one keyword that appears in no PDF text, so hits can only come from the comment. Write down for each step: found / not found, and whether you could tell which chapter it was.\n\n- [ ] Search box (toolbar), scope \"All\", type the unique keyword → does the parent record show up? (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Same with the search scope set to Comments only (search options menu), if available in your version\n- [ ] Search operator: `comment:\"value form\"` in the search field → parent found?\n- [ ] Search for a keyword that is also in the PDF text: is the parent listed once, and is it clear that the keyword matched the comment, not only the text?\n- [ ] Does the result tell you which chapter the keyword belongs to without opening the Inspector? (expected: no, only the block in the comment says so)\n- [ ] Search for a phrase of two words in chapter A's keywords that are in different blocks (`value` from A and `money` from B): do you get a false match for the parent?\n- [ ] Smart Group with rule \"Comment contains\" `-- sp-chapter: KEY --` → lists the parent records that carry chapter blocks; useful as a to-do view?\n- [ ] Tag browser and `tags:value form`: confirm the keyword is not there (intended)\n- [ ] Search from Emacs, if #418 is merged (`C-c k d f` with the keyword): do the parent records appear? (skip if #418 is not on your branch)\n- [ ] Verdict for the PR thread: good enough with comments only, or do you want the prefixed-tag fallback (`ch:KEY/keyword`)?\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 441-devonthink-chapter-keywords`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- DEVONthink: open the parent record's Comment in the inspector and delete the `-- sp-chapter: KEY --` … `-- end sp-chapter --` block(s) you created (nothing else was written), and remove any Smart Group you made for the test. In a litnote, drop the `* Keywords in the …` section or `git -C ~/notes restore .` if the vault is under git.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC\n",
